---
/**
 * The two vertical gutter rules at the edges of the content column
 * (x=160 and x=1352 at the 1512 design width).
 *
 * These deliberately do *not* live in GridFrame any more: GridFrame carries the
 * section's vertical padding, so rules drawn inside it stopped short of the
 * section edges and left a gap wherever two sections met. This is a sibling
 * overlay pinned to the section box instead, so the rules run edge to edge.
 *
 * Place it as a direct child of a `relative` section. Dark sections only —
 * on light sections the frame is not drawn at all.
 *
 * Below `md` the rules are hidden; at that width they would eat the viewport.
 */
---

<div
  aria-hidden="true"
  class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-1/2 z-0 hidden w-full max-w-[var(--content-width)] -translate-x-1/2 md:block"
>
  <span class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 w-px bg-rule"></span>
  <span class="absolute inset-y-0 right-0 w-px bg-rule"></span>
</div>
